# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you need. Everything here is optional:
# with nothing set, Speedex runs fully in the browser against Cloudflare.

# ── Prediction model ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the model API. The app POSTs to <url>/predict.
# Leave unset to use the built-in heuristic estimate.
# "/api" goes through the Vite dev proxy below (no CORS needed locally).
# VITE_PREDICTION_API_URL=/api

# Where the dev proxy forwards /api requests (dev server only).
# MODEL_API_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# ── Packet loss (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Packet loss needs a TURN relay. Point this at an endpoint that returns
# {"username": "...", "credential": "..."} for Cloudflare Realtime TURN,
# e.g. the turn-worker example in github.com/cloudflare/speedtest.
# VITE_TURN_CREDS_URL=https://your-worker.example.workers.dev/turn-credentials
# VITE_TURN_SERVER_URI=turn.cloudflare.com:3478
